+# Bridge intake residue — the pre-stall cohort was never drained (extends #1987)
+
+Report-only. Extends `docs/reports/BRIDGE_INTAKE_STALL_2026-10-28.md` (#1987, landed `232179f`),
+which triaged the intake verdict stall for WOs **queued 01:55–05:14Z** and proposed recipes
+R1–R4. That window excluded everything submitted **before 01:55Z**. Verified at open-main tip
+`97bb269` (2026-10-28T08:55Z): the older cohort is still in-gates with zero verdicts —
+**9–18 h after submission** — while the gate pipeline demonstrably recovered for all newer
+traffic. The stall ended; the residue did not.
+
+## Cohort (all five evidence rows verified live 2026-10-28T09:02Z)
+
+| PR | WO | PR created (UTC) | age @09:02Z | WO state | verdict | head branch on origin | content on main |
+|----|----|------------------|-------------|----------|---------|----------------------|-----------------|
+| #336 | #1472 | 10-27T14:36:09Z | ~18.4 h | open, `bridge:in-gates` | `""` | present (`passkey-imports-svc`) | absent |
+| #339 | #1817 | 10-27T23:49:00Z | ~9.2 h | **closed** | `""` | **absent** | absent |
+| #341 | #1813 | 10-27T23:49:21Z | ~9.2 h | **closed** | `""` | **absent** | absent |
+| #343 | #1786 | 10-27T23:49:57Z | ~9.2 h | open, `bridge:in-gates` | `""` | present (`lease-ssot-wiring`) | absent |
+| #345 | #1770 | 10-27T23:50:11Z | ~9.2 h | open, `bridge:in-gates` | `""` | present (`dependabot-lane-dossier`) | absent |
+
+Evidence commands (all reproducible):
+- `gh pr list` (tower `github_list_prs`): all five `state=open`, `updatedAt == createdAt`
+  (no surface movement since submission).
+- `bridge_read_feedback {"number": N}` for 1472/1786/1813/1817/1770: `latestVerdict.verdict`
+  is the **empty string** for all five; #1813/#1817 are `state=closed` **without any verdict
+  stamp**; #1472/#1786/#1770 remain `bridge:in-gates`.
+- `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/*`: `pii-gap-eval` and `run9-wo1792-parity-schedule` head
+  refs are **not advertised** while their PRs (#339/#341) remain open — an inconsistent head
+  state (fork-head or stale advertisement; #1987's R1 discriminator applies as-is).
+- `git log origin/main --all --grep=<slug>` for `passkey|pii-gap|parity-schedule|lease-ssot|dependabot-lane`:
+  **zero content landings** (only unrelated R37 dependabot-gate work shares the token).
+- Recovery contrast: main cascade `94008df → 97bb269` landed eight newer bridge PRs
+  (#2050/#2052/#2055/#2057/#2061/#2063/#2066/#2068) between 02:50–08:55Z — the pipeline works
+  for traffic it sees; it never came back to this cohort.
+
+## Why this is a distinct surface (not #1987, not #2025)
+
+1. **Not #1987**: that record's scope line is explicit — "20 WOs queued 01:55–05:14Z". The
+   cohort predates the window (14:36Z and 23:49–23:50Z on 10-27). Its R3 backfill recipe was
+   applied forward; nothing revisited the pre-window queue.
+2. **Not #2025** (verdict backfill stamps FALSE rejections): this cohort has **no verdicts at
+   all**, plus a new sub-defect — **WO closed without any verdict while its PR stays open**
+   (#1813/#1817). Closed WOs vanish from the open-queue metric (the same metric #1987 already
+   flagged as unsound), so the residue is *invisible* to board-driven pickers: an agent
+   re-reading the queue cannot even discover that #1813/#1817 ever existed.
+3. **Active harm, not passive staleness**: the lane's own anti-stampede audit trips on *stale
+   open ancestors* (a6 receipt `469ddb8`, 5th trigger class). Five stale open PRs are exactly
+   that class — every future submitter in overlapping scopes risks a guard trip caused purely
+   by residue. WO #1770 is a concrete victim-in-waiting: its dossier scope (dependabot lane)
+   is a standing admin thread, and a future re-cert PR will collide with the ghost.
+
+## Admin recipes (numbered to continue #1987's R-series)
+
+- **R5 (drain)**: re-run the gate evaluator over PRs #336/#339/#341/#343/#345 against current
+  main; stamp real verdicts (APPLIED → squash-merge, REJECTED → close with reason). Five PRs,
+  none merged, no conflicts expected for the three docs-only dossiers.
+- **R6 (de-orphan)**: for #1813/#1817 either reopen the WOs (verdict-adjacent state must not
+  bypass the queue metric) or stamp terminal verdicts on them AND close their PRs. WO-closed +
+  PR-open + verdict-empty is an invalid terminal state triple — add it to the watchdog.
+- **R7 (age guard)**: `bridge_landing_watchdog` gains an `IN_GATES_AGE` classification:
+  WO labeled `bridge:in-gates` with `now - latestVerdict.at > 4 h` (or PR age > 4 h with empty
+  verdict) → alert lane. Proposal only — implementation is a maintainer decision (#1987 R4
+  already owns the watchdog metric slot; R7 composes with it).
+
+## Boundary
+
+Docs-only, single new file, zero code touched, no protected paths. Honest absence: the two
+absent head branches are reported as observed (not advertised by origin); root-causing *why*
+(fork-head vs deletion race) needs admin-side PR internals this lane cannot read.
